From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SpreadZhao <spreadzhao@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:18:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bar/barcolors: support status text color markup

Support ^fg(RRGGBB), ^bg(RRGGBB), ^fg() and ^bg() markers in status text
without counting markup toward text width or click areas.

Color syntax follows barcolors by Kerberoge:
https://codeberg.org/dwl/dwl-patches/src/branch/main/patches/barcolors
---
 README.md |  4 +++
 dwl.1     | 12 +++++++++
 dwl.c     | 79 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 93 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 000a4f6..a82d676 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -113,6 +113,10 @@ Every output shows the latest complete line. Lines may contain up to 1023 bytes,
 excluding the newline. Overlong lines are discarded and the previous status is
 preserved. The startup command does not receive status information.
 
+Status text supports `^fg(RRGGBB)` and `^bg(RRGGBB)` to change foreground and
+background colors. `^fg()` and `^bg()` restore the normal colors. Invalid markers
+are displayed as text.
+
 ### (Known) Java nonreparenting WM issue
 Certain IDEs don't display correctly unless an environmental variable for Java AWT
 indicates that the WM is nonreparenting.
